      {
        "id": "1",
        "kind": "comment",
        "config": {
          "text": "A synth that talks. Press Space to play.\n\nThe Vocoder block splits two signals into twelve matching bands: the carrier (a sawtooth chord, what you hear) and the modulator (a voice, what it says). Each band of the carrier is turned up and down by the level of the same band in the modulator, so the chord takes on the voice's vowels and rhythm. Here the voice is a little robot built from parts; switch on Use Audio In and talk into a microphone to make the chord say your words."
        },
